{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509039-blending-in-forsaken","id":1509039,"title":"Blending in Forsaken?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-20T08:42:15-07:00","id":1509039,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon4.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Blending in Forsaken?","content":"I was a little surprised by something in the preview for W5:<ul><li>Werewolves belong to multiple worlds - flesh, wolf, and spirit - but are wholly accepted by none.</li> </ul>This seems a little odd to me - wasn't this only the case in Forsaken? Pretty sure in Apocalypse they didn't have this conflict.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T09:50:01-07:00","id":1509051,"title":"","content":"Well, it depends on the degree....<br /> <br /> Generally it was often mentioned that aspects of Forsaken are being incorporated in W5.<br /> <br /> That said, what does wolf, flesh and spirit even mean?<br /> Is a wolf its own kind of being, like mushrooms having aspects of animal and plant cells in their cells?<br /> Between flesh and spirit there is wolf. The hidden sphere the mages search for.....<br /> <br /> Just kidding.<br /> <br /> WtA had aspects of possibly a longing for something beyond the physical world. A theme that especially in Theurge characters might be something to explore. But it was never the main focus of the game. The ToJ sourcebook &quot;Apocalypse&quot; mentioned that WtA was about the physical world, and finding salvation in the spirit realms, or even a new Gaia, was not the theme of the game.<br /> <br /> It has also been discussed a lot, that Garou are not part of the human world. The Curse is key here. But the world of flesh, or matter I'd guess, is still very much their world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T10:36:57-07:00","id":1509063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509039-blending-in-forsaken#post1509039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was a little surprised by something in the preview for W5:<ul><li>Werewolves belong to multiple worlds - flesh, wolf, and spirit - but are wholly accepted by none.</li> </ul>This seems a little odd to me - wasn't this only the case in Forsaken? Pretty sure in Apocalypse they didn't have this conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forsaken 1st Edition is the only Werewolf Edition that the lead developer for W5 liked, it stands to reason he'd be blending in as much as possible ( despite WtF 2nd Edition being far superior and trying to combine WtA and WtF lessening the themes and strengths of both games and ultimately leading to WtF being suffocated by the current IP holders,,,,,Oops.....*steps off of Rant-Box*)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T10:41:27-07:00","id":1509065,"title":"","content":"I always thought of Garou as Human+Spirit+wolf, they are not half and half, they are simply more, and the same goes for the other splats. I think Garou being MORE is really integral to their being. It gives them their much needed arrogance as a chosen warrior race, setting them up to be tragic heroes rather than just tragedies. From an outside perspective it posits the idea that the rage-phobia of mundane humans being the result of a spiritual deficit while other supernaturals can bear it. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm hoping the line is more Toreador style posturing than actual information we're supposed to treat as objective, but I have little hope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T11:37:15-07:00","id":1509070,"title":"","content":"Garou were always part spirit, it was just less important than with the Uratha. Forsaken is about the relationship between the human and spirit worlds, and thus the Uratha being half-spirit is very important, whereas Werewolf cares much more about the physical world than the spirit one even if the two are linked. Hell you can even take a background for greater spirit heritage.<br /> <br /> Although Garou did always have the human/wolf conflict, which Uratha don't really have (they're much more firmly on the human side, except for maybe Predator Kings). Homids, lupus, and Metis don't view the world in the same way, with the Glasswalkers and Red Talons taking this to extremes, but it's not meant to be the major focus of the game.<br /> <br /> That's not to say that JA hasn't taken a lot from 1e Forsaken, because he clearly has. Even beyond his personal preferences WW seems to be gutting CofD to try and shove the best bits into WoD (which can just fail miserably, Blood Potency in Masquerade just doesn't work). Disappointment in WoD5 doing that is half the reason I picked up CofD again (the other reasons being the lack of releases and wow do the WoD5 rules suck).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T11:41:52-07:00","id":1509071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It makes me wonder if we'll see another jarring tonal shift in future books as a result.</div> </div> </div> </div>V5 shifted massively with the departure of Ericsson and then again after Sj\u00f6gren departed. Its fairly likely it will do so again now that Achilli is gone. Though Muammer is still there, he seemed to butt heads with Achilli fairly often according to certain freelancers so maybe he'll take the chance to ' course correct', though from recollection he's very much a Vampire guy and only sees W5 as an addition to V5 rather than its own thing.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T11:50:43-07:00","id":1509073,"title":"","content":"What I found even odder is that &quot;Werewolves belong to multiple worlds - flesh, wolf, and spirit - but are wholly accepted by none.&quot; is followed up by &quot;Werewolves are feared and mistrusted by each of the worlds to which they partially belong&quot;... I mean, this is just the same thing phrased in two different ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T12:15:08-07:00","id":1509075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509039-blending-in-forsaken?p=1509073#post1509073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I found even odder is that &quot;Werewolves belong to multiple worlds - flesh, wolf, and spirit - but are wholly accepted by none.&quot; is followed up by &quot;Werewolves are feared and mistrusted by each of the worlds to which they partially belong&quot;... I mean, this is just the same thing phrased in two different ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not unusual there are parts of the Sabbat book and Players Guide that have entire paragraphs following each other that are identical in meaning with just the syntax altered. It's particularly prominent in parts of the PG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T13:02:59-07:00","id":1509080,"title":"","content":"There was a duality in Apocalypse but the kind of distrust that the inhabitants of the Hisil have for the Forsaken is nothing like the relationship that the Garou had to Naturae. That would be a rather notable departure from what was, if they tried to push the Forsaken setup on Apocalypse. Also, there's the thing about the reunion of the spirit and material being pretty much unequivocally good in W:tA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T18:14:48-07:00","id":1509125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even &quot;Forsaken setup&quot; is a stretch. There are certain bespoke aspects to Forsaken and what the Uratha are in their own world that just doesn't exist or exist the way it does in WoD like in CofD. So at best I'd be squinting my eyes again at concepts squeezed into 5e WoD that doesn't feel like it's really being down with an eye towards the overall picture.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recall that Changing Ways tried to cram in First Tongue terms. It didn't seem to last.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T00:12:37-07:00","id":1509142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509039-blending-in-forsaken?p=1509080#post1509080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was a duality in Apocalypse but the kind of distrust that the inhabitants of the Hisil have for the Forsaken is nothing like the relationship that the Garou had to Naturae. That would be a rather notable departure from what was, if they tried to push the Forsaken setup on Apocalypse. Also, there's the thing about the reunion of the spirit and material being pretty much unequivocally good in W:tA.</div> </div> </div> </div>The focus seems to be on Garou not really understanding how anything works and that combined with the idea that due to their Rage they always are at risk of losing themselves, they have become feared and mistrusted by both mortals and spirits. Like, under the Truths-section they talk about how Garou think the &quot;Wyrm is the biggest threat and they're all about confronting its agents, real or <i>imagined</i>.&quot; Or how the Umbra-part in the &quot;What do werewolves do&quot;-section is about &quot;exploring the <i>mysteries </i>of the Umbra&quot; for which the basis is yet another instance of Garou not fully understanding something.<br /> <br /> Still don't really feel like this fits with Garou-society supposedly being this ancient thing that has existed since the dawn of time but oh well...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T06:16:22-07:00","id":1509172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509039-blending-in-forsaken?p=1509071#post1509071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its fairly likely it will do so again now that Achilli is gone.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank the gods!<br /> <br /> (...but the damage has already been done.. by a significant amount)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T15:05:03-07:00","id":1509319,"title":"","content":"I've played with idea of using the ivory claws, fire touched and balehounds as additional wyrm tribes to put a more werewolf vs werewolf spin on the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T19:17:59-07:00","id":1509338,"title":"","content":"I don't see why not. It's just a game-idea; the only real difference is the rules. Once, I did run a Werewolf: Dark Ages game set in ancient Roman-times; it was tribe v. tribe and all the Apocalypse etc, was not there. Romans, that were big, hairy with claws and fangs (verse, just fangs).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}